 page; use a fresh home to test the newly built bundled view. To explicitly update
 a stored page, use `jelly --url http://127.0.0.1:17850 reshape surface --view assets/surface.html`
 from the checkout, merging these changes into any customized view first.
+
+# Comment Escape browser check
+
+Requires Cargo, Chrome and `playwright-cli`. From the checkout, build and start a
+fresh throwaway daemon, then create the map fixture in another terminal:
+
+```sh
+cargo build --locked --target-dir /tmp/jelly-escape-target
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly serve --port 17883 --home /tmp/jelly-escape-home
+# In another terminal, from the checkout:
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly --url http://127.0.0.1:17883 new escape:map \
+  --view skill/recipes/map/view.html --verbs skill/recipes/map/verbs.js --state skill/recipes/map/state.json
+```
+
+Run from a scratch directory with the absolute path to the script:
+
+```sh
+playwright-cli -s=escape open http://127.0.0.1:17883/
+playwright-cli -s=escape run-code --filename=/path/to/jelly/tests/comment-escape.js
+playwright-cli -s=escape close
+```
+
+The check exercises Escape in standalone and embedded maps, including comment
+editor cancellation and ordinary trace dismissal. It fails with the pre-fix
+runtime. Stop the throwaway daemon afterward; use a fresh home for each run.
